gwaihirj@yahoo.com (Rachel Jacobs) writes:
> Is Slow Monster cumulative?

Monsters have three speed modifiers; fast, normal, and slow. All
monsters start at normal, with the exception of bats, giant bats, and
vampire bats created in Gehennom, which start at fast. Speed monster
bumps them up a level, and slow monster down a level, but they won't
get faster than fast (4/3 base speed) or slower than slow (2/3 base
speed). Monsters wearing speed boots are always fast regardless of
their intrinsic speed modifier.

(Those figures are rough; there's a couple of fudges to counter
rounding problems. And there are a fair number of other effects that
will bump the modifiers in one direction or another; spells,
golem-zapping, lifesaved petrification, slowing attacks, etc.)

